    {
      "id": "cf545d77-0db6-4142-9cef-63e034f867d3",
      "name": "Sticky Note7",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2528,
        1856
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1520,
        "height": 2000,
        "content": "AI-Driven Recruitment and ATS Pipeline\n\nThis workflow automates resume screening and evaluation using AI to improve candidate processing and reduce manual HR effort.\nThis workflow is ideal for HR teams and recruiters who want to streamline candidate screening by combining form submissions, resume parsing, job description matching, and AI evaluation into a single, automated process.\n\nHow it works:\n1. A candidate submits their application using a form that includes name, email, CV (PDF), and a selected job role.\n2. The CV is uploaded to Google Drive for record-keeping and later reference.\n3. The Profile Analyzer Agent reads the uploaded resume, extracts structured candidate information, and transforms it into a standardized JSON format using GPT and a custom output parser.\n4. The corresponding job description PDF file is automatically retrieved from a Google Sheet based on the selected job role.\n5. The HR Expert Agent evaluates the candidate profile against the job description using another GPT model, generating a structured assessment that includes strengths, gaps, and an overall recommendation.\n6. The evaluation result is parsed and formatted for output.\n7. The evaluation score will be used to mark candidate as qualified or unqualified. Based on that an email will be sent to applicant or the message will be send to hiring team for the next process.\n8. The final evaluation result will be stored in a Google Sheet for long-term tracking and reporting.\n\nRequirements:\n1. OpenAI account for both Profile Analyzer and HR Expert Agents\n2. Google Drive account (for storing CVs and evaluation sheet)\n3. Google Sheets API credentials (for JD source and evaluation results)"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
